FORM ID BeamForm AT (2 62 156 96)
USABLE
MODAL
DEFAULTBTNID btn_beam_done
BEGIN
  TITLE "Beam Stuff..."
  LABEL "To beam kMoria, tap kMoria and" AUTOID AT (4 15)
  LABEL "it will be sent in two pieces." AUTOID AT (PrevLeft PrevBottom)
  LABEL "You can also share your top score." AUTOID AT (PrevLeft PrevBottom)
  BUTTON "kMoria" ID btn_beam_myself AT (5 58 AUTO AUTO)
  BUTTON "Top Score" ID btn_beam_scores AT (PrevRight+6 PrevTop AUTO AUTO)
  BUTTON "Item" ID btn_beam_item AT (5 PrevTop+20 AUTO AUTO)
  BUTTON "Cash" ID btn_beam_cash AT (PrevRight+6 PrevTop AUTO AUTO) NONUSABLE
  BUTTON "Done" ID btn_beam_done AT (PrevRight+6 PrevTop 35 AUTO)
END

FORM ID BeamCashForm AT (2 63 156 95)
USABLE
MODAL
BEGIN
  TITLE "Beam Cash"
  FIELD ID field_bc AT (5 59 80 11) EDITABLE UNDERLINED SINGLELINE MAXCHARS 8
  BUTTON "Ok" ID btn_bc_ok AT (5 78 AUTO AUTO)
  BUTTON "Cancel" ID btn_bc_cancel AT (PrevRight+5 PrevTop AUTO AUTO)
END


FORM ID UserForm AT (0 0 160 160)
USABLE
DEFAULTBTNID btn_user_cancel
BEGIN
  TITLE "Switch Users"
  LIST "foo" "bar" "baz" ID list_user AT (1 15 158 55)
  BUTTON "Ok" ID btn_user_ok AT (2 147 35 AUTO)
  BUTTON "New" ID btn_user_new AT (PrevRight+5 PrevTop 35 AUTO)
  BUTTON "Cancel" ID btn_user_cancel AT (PrevRight+5 PrevTop AUTO AUTO)
  CHECKBOX "Hotsync?" ID check_user_1 AT (2 PrevTop-15 AUTO AUTO) NONUSABLE
END








STRING AboutStr "kMoria version 0.16 (24 Nov 2026)\n"\
                "© 2000 Bridget Spitznagel, James Wilson, Robert Koeneke.\n"\
                "This program was derived "\
                "from UMoria 5.5.2.\n\n"\
                "kMoria comes with Absolutely No Warranty.\n"\
                "kMoria is freeware.  You can redistribute it "\
                "and/or modify it (provided that "\
                "this notice and the full credits are retained), but "\
                "it CANNOT be distributed for profit."\
                "\n\nVersion 0.16 (2026) updates 0.15 for "\
                "current Palm OS devices and build tools.  "\
                "Source and bug reports: "\
                "github.com/z88kat/palm-roguelike"

STRING CreditStr "Moria has been around since 1983.  "\
		"(The Mines of Moria, and the Balrog dwelling therein, come "\
		"from _The Lord of the Rings_ by J.R.R. Tolkien.)  "\
		"The game of Moria was created by Robert Alan Koeneke "\
		"with assistants Jimmey Wayne Todd and Gary D. McAdoo.  "\
		"It has many descendants.  "\
		"kMoria is a port of Umoria 5.5.2 which is itself "\
		"descended in varying degree from:\n"\
		"UNIX Port a.k.a. Umoria 4.x (James E. Wilson),\n"\
		"MSDOS Port (Don Kneller),\n"\
		"BRUCE Moria (Christopher Stuart),\n"\
		"Amiga Port (Corey Gehman).\n"\
		"Umoria 5.5.x is maintained by David Grabiner.\n\n"\
		"I, Bridget Spitznagel, ported it to PalmOS.\n"\
		"Celebrimbor of Hollin drew these signs (no, not really)."

STRING DeathStr "If you do not want to create a memo just press the "\
		"Next Page button to go on.\n\n"\
		"The Write Memo button will write your Character Record "\
		"to a new memo in your Memo Pad application.  "\
		"This memo will be Unfiled category and will have the "\
		"time and date of character death in its title.  "\
		"The Character Record has the same format as in Unix Moria "\
		"and will look better on an 80-column display than "\
		"on your PalmOS device.  Sync the memo to your computer "\
		"and then you can archive it, show it off, or garner "\
		"sympathy for a near-win just as on any other platform."

// Note: Fix this string, because it is a lie.
// Actually the (i) does not appear in those forms, maybe due to not modal.
STRING CharGenStr "Welcome to Moria!\nYour first task "\
	"is to generate a character.  You must specify a sex, a race, "\
	"and a class.  \n"\
	"If this is your first time playing, you may want to "\
	"read the manual first."

STRING InstructStr "You are an adventurer seeking to defeat the Balrog "\
	"which lurks in the deeper levels of the Dungeons of Moria.  "\
	"You may acquire supplies on the town level.  Move by tapping "\
	"on the screen.  Other commands are listed in the menus; for "\
	"example, write i to access your inventory.\nFor more "\
	"help, see <github.com/z88kat/palm-roguelike>."

STRING InvHelpStr "Tap any inventory item to select it.  "\
	"A set of buttons will appear.  "\
	"Tap a button to perform an action.  "\
	"(Note: Each action takes time!)  "\
	"Tap Done to exit the inventory screen, or "\
	"tap [E] to visit the equipment screen.\n\n"\
	"If you are in a store, you will see a 'sell' button "\
	"only if the store is willing to buy that type of item; "\
	"some other actions may also be possible."

STRING EquHelpStr "Tap any equipped item to select it.  "\
	"A set of buttons will appear.  "\
	"Tap a button to perform an action.  "\
	"(Note: Each action takes time!)  "\
	"Tap Done to exit the equipment screen, or "\
	"tap [In] to visit the inventory screen."

STRING StoreHelpStr "To buy an item from the store list, select the item "\
	"and tap Buy.  To sell an item from your inventory, tap Sell.  "\
	"To view the next page of items offered by this store (if any), "\
	"tap [+>].  The number between these two paging buttons will "\
	"indicate the page you are on.  Tap Exit to leave the store." \
	"\n\nTo buy or sell an item, you must negotiate a price with "\
	"the store owner.  Write your offer, or tap [=] to match his "\
	"offer.  Or, use the [+n] autoincrement button which appears after "\
	"you have made at least two offers (n is the difference between "\
	"your two most recent offers); tap the button to extrapolate a "\
	"new offer."\
	"\nThen tap Submit."

STRING BookHelpStr "Select the book that contains the spell/prayer that "\
	"you wanted to use."

STRING SpellHelpStr "This is the list of spells/prayers in the book that "\
	"you are currently reading.  Each has a level (Lv), mana requirement "\
	"(Mn), and a probability of casting failure (Fail).  \n"\
	"To recite a spell/prayer, select it and tap Recite; "\
	"or tap Close Book to cancel and return to your list of books."

STRING GainSpellHelpStr "Each spell/prayer has a level (Lv), mana "\
	"requirement (Mn), and a probability of casting failure (Fail).  \n"\
	"- If you're here to Gain Spells: "\
	"Select a spell that appeals to you and tap Learn. "\
	"When you can learn no more, or you do not like the "\
	"remaining choices, tap Done.\n"\
	"- If you are just Browsing: "\
	"you can Toggle between Lv-Mn-Fail and Status "\
	"(tells you whether each listed spell/prayer is unknown to you, "\
	"whether you have not tried it yet, etc.)" 

STRING PrefsHelpStr "Hole & Donut: set the size of the movement donut.  (Turn Circles on and Relative Move off, if you want to see it overlaid on the dungeon.) \n\n"\
"Big font: set the default font to large (or small)\n"\
"Relative move: center the donut around your @ (or center of screen)\n"\
"Circles: draw the donut on the screen (or don't); but, this only works when Relative Move is turned off\n"\
"Sound: turn the sound on (or off)\n"\
"Run: tapping outside the donut will run (or will walk)\n"\
"Cut known corners: when running in a passage, use diagonal movement to save time (or don't)\n"\
"Examine potential corners: when running in an unexplored passage, do not move diagonally (or do leave corners unexplored)\n"\
"Stop when map sector changes: stop running when you enter a new screen (or keep going)\n"\
"Run through open doors: don't stop at doors (or stop so you can close 'em)\n"\
"Prompt to pick up objects: no effect, not implemented yet\n"\
"Highlight mineral seams: display softer rock walls as % and harder rock as #"


STRING ButtonsStr "You can re-bind hardware buttons at whim, more or less. "\
		"Your settings will be remembered but will not be USED "\
		"unless you check 'rebind these buttons'.  "\
		"Anything set to '---' will just do what it normally would.  "
